<title>USA: Three firms win Air Force planes support work.</title>
<headline>Three firms win Air Force planes support work.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Air Force announced Wednesday that three companies will share a $190 million contract to provide support services for a variety of planes and helicopters.</p>
<p>It said it awarded the contract to Adroit Systems of Alexandria, Va.; Modern Technologies Corp. of Dayton, Ohio, and Support Systems Associates, Inc. of Hauppauge, N.Y.</p>
